### Relevant Files

1. `internal/task/service.go`: `StartTask`, `CompleteTask`, `update`, `closeSubtasksWith` and `runAutoArchive` are where status writes happen and where the lock is held.
2. `internal/tools/workflow.go`: the MCP handlers, which have `ctx` and control the post-complete auto-archive call.
3. `internal/config/config.go`: the config struct, `DefaultConfig`, `applyDefaults`, `applyEnvOverrides` and the root resolution that decides which directory git would run in.
4. `internal/storage/markdown.go`: `Save` and `parse` frontmatter structs that must be extended for any new persisted field.
5. `internal/task/task.go`: the Task model and the resolution helpers (`Delivered`).
6. `internal/storage/index.go`: the in-memory index and its mtime/count self-healing, which reacts to checkouts that rewrite `tasks/` files.
7. `internal/cli/commands.go` and `internal/cli/cli.go`: the CLI `start`/`complete` share the service path but not the auto-archive call.
8. `internal/task/concurrency_test.go`: the twin-discipline guard every new exported Service method must be added to.
9. `internal/testsupport/testsupport.go`: the temp backlog helpers; root equals tasks dir there.
10. `internal/tools/descriptions/{start_task,complete_task}.yaml` and `internal/app/instructions.md`: the agent-facing text that documents the workflow.
11. `skills/superpowers-workflow/SKILL.md` (and its `plugins/` mirror): the only existing skill that runs git around `complete_task`.

### Inference

- **Task-file writes dirty the working tree.** `tasks/` is tracked and `update` writes `{id}.md` on every start and complete. So in this repo a `start_task` or `complete_task` status write, and any auto-archive rename, is itself an uncommitted change inside the git worktree. This is an inference from `git ls-files` showing 92 tracked files under `tasks/`, from `internal/task/service.go:478` and from `internal/storage/markdown.go:87-96`. Whether other projects track `.tasks/` is project-specific.
- **A checkout will trigger an index rebuild.** Git writes checked-out files with a fresh mtime, which is after `builtAt`, and file count changes are also detected. The zero-directory case is the exception (`internal/storage/index.go:220-222`). This is inferred from git's standard checkout behaviour; no test in the repo exercises a checkout.
- **Tests with real git need two things.** First, a repo created in `t.TempDir()`, because no existing helper creates one. Second, an identity configured per repo or through env, because there is no CI test job and git identity on test machines cannot be assumed. This is inferred from the absence of any git usage in `*.go` and from `.github/workflows/release.yml`.
- **`git config user.name` is not branch-safe as is.** `Igor Karatayev` contains a space, and git refnames cannot contain spaces (git-check-ref-format rules, external to the repo).

### Unknown

- Which git identity field should become `<git.user>` (name slug, email local part, or a config value), and how to slugify it. This is not determined by the code; it is a design decision.
- Whether the resolved root should be required to equal the git toplevel or only be inside a worktree. Resolution can yield a root that is a subdirectory, the parent of an absolute `MCP_TASKS_DIR`, or a non-repo (`internal/config/config.go:163-167,308-312`).
- How `update_task(status: in_progress|done)` should interact with branching, since it bypasses `StartTask` and `CompleteTask` (`internal/tools/management.go:270-294`).
- Whether non-delivered resolutions (obsolete, wontfix, ...) and the subtask cascade or parent auto-complete should trigger branch operations (`internal/task/service.go:654-689`).
- Whether auto-archive renames that happen right after `complete_task` (`internal/tools/workflow.go:99-100`) should go into the squashed commit or stay outside it.
- Whether the in-progress `superpowers-workflow` skill, which commits on the current branch after `complete_task` (`skills/superpowers-workflow/SKILL.md:340-344`), would conflict with server-side branch switching when the feature is enabled.
- How to handle the current task `git-branch-per-task`: it is already `in_progress` on `main_patched`, before any branching exists, so it has no recorded start commit.
